# Auto commit and push

Whenever you make meaningful code changes in this repository:

1. Create a git commit for those changes (follow the project's commit message style).
2. Immediately push the commit to the tracked remote branch (`git push` / `git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
3. Do this without waiting for the user to ask again — the user has explicitly requested automatic push after changes.
4. Never force-push to `main`/`master` unless the user explicitly requests it.
5. Do not commit secrets, `.env`, credentials, or unrelated local Cursor config unless the user asks.
6. Do not commit agent-only guidance, personal checklists, or instructions the user said were "for you only" — keep those outside the repo (e.g. user-level Cursor rules).
